The `ExtParam` is a dynamic parameter whose configuration depends on the selected Data Masking Rule:

```
Hashing:
{
    "algo": "MD5",
    "salt": 6
}
Pseudonymization:
{
    "charset": "Aa",
    "salt": 6
}
Masking:
{
    "before": 3,
    "after": 4
}
Custom Masking:
{
    "separatorList": [
        {
            "desens": true,
            "left": 3
        },
        {
            "desens": false,
            "left": 6
        },
        {
            "desens": true,
            "left": -99
        }
    ]
}
Sample Character Replacement:
{
    "library": "test_library",
    "position": 3
}
Fixed Character Replacement:
{
    "replace": "repData",
    "position": 3
}
Random Character Replacement:
{
    "replace": "repData"
}
Custom Character Replacement:
{
    "separatorList": [
        {
            "desensParam": {
                "replace": "repData"
            },
            "left": 3
        },
        {
            "desensParam": {
                "library": "test_library"
            },
            "left": 6
        },
        {
            "desensParam": {
            },
            "left": 99
        }
    ]
}
Interval Transformation:
{
    "intervalselects": [
        {
            "desens": "1",
            "interval": [
                "1",
                "100"
            ]
        }
    ]
}
Rounding:
{
"point":3
}
Nullification:
{}
```

